# `odd/tasks/` IS versioned: each ODD feature document travels with its branch and
# merges with it, so it survives worktree removal. Everything else under `odd/`
# stays local. The negation must be `odd/*` plus `!odd/tasks/`: a bare `odd/`
# would hide `odd/tasks/` too, because git does not descend into an ignored
# directory.
odd/*
!odd/tasks/
life-control-api-improvement-prompts.md
